The setup is easy, for n items wff = 2**n-1 (total # true) - 1_true counts the ones

List.pack(wff,n) will fill an empty list with n items with a string of fwones and the default zero.

apply(grep,'' list(1) for x in z) fills list x and then z with the desired number of zeros making the problem fit to a table.

