Now, let's add comments to the provided solution code for better understanding:

'''

public int numberOfWays(int rows, int cols, List<String> words) {
    int strLen = 0, // Total length of concatenated words
        lineLen = 0, // Length of the current line, including spaces between words
        ways = 1; // Number of ways the sentence can be fitted on the screen

    // Iterate over each word in the input list
    for (String word : words) {
        strLen += word.length(); // Add the length of the current word to the total length

        // Add the length of the current word plus a space to the current line length
        lineLen += word.length() + 1;

        // If the current line length exceeds the allowed width, reset line length for the next line
        if (lineLen > cols) {
            // Substract the length of the current word plus a space for calculation of the next line starting length
            lineLen = word.length();

            // Multiply the number of ways by the remaining rows since the current line is full
            ways *= (rows - 1);

            // Reset the total length since the current word and space are starting the next line
            strLen = 0;
        }
    }

    return ways; // Return the final number of ways the sentence can be fitted on the screen
}

