You are given a string $$$s$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters.

You can perform the following operation on $$$s$$$:

Choose any two indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ such that $$$1 \le i \lt j \le n$$$ and swap the characters at positions $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$.

Your task is to find the lexicographically smallest string that you can obtain by applying the above operation at most $$$k$$$ times.

Input
The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ (1 \le n \le 10^5, 1 \le k \le 10^9).

The second line contains $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters.

Output
