This code uses bit manipulation to generate all possible sets of branches that can be closed. For each set, it checks if the remaining branches are still reachable from each other within the maximum distance. If they are, it increments the result counter. The code uses a breadth-first search (BFS) algorithm to calculate the distances between branches.

